<!--
    Cloud SuperApp — first translated locale. Until this file the app had only
    values/ and values-sw600dp/, so its entire interface rendered in English on
    a phone set to Spanish. The note above status_light_on in values/strings.xml
    asked for exactly this file, by exactly this name.

    WHY values-es AND NOT values-es-rES. The device asks for Spanish (Spain).
    Android answers that request by looking for values-es-rES first and then
    falling back to the language-only values-es, so both directories reach this
    phone — but values-es also reaches es-MX, es-AR and every other Spanish
    region, and values-es-rES reaches none of them. ac_cloud-mail already ships
    values-es and the owner reads that app in Spanish today, which is the
    working proof that this device consults this directory.

    english_ime_name is absent on purpose: it is translatable="false" in
    values/, because it is the keyboard's name in Settings and must stay
    "Cloud Keyboard" in every locale.

    TERMS DELIBERATELY LEFT IN ENGLISH, because this interface is read by a
    systems engineer who says them in English and a Spanish word for them would
    read as a different concept: peer, mesh, overlay, snapshot, backend, topic,
    feed, commit, stack, workflow, endpoint, token, tag, WireGuard, ntfy, GHCR,
    JSON, APK, TOTP, CalDAV, Drive, Vault, Wallet, Linktree, Mattermost.
    Identifiers quoted from configuration (build.json::ui.control_panel,
    cloud-data, versionCode, the `samples` key) are literal and are not touched.
-->
